# Visual-storyboard frames: regenerable review artifacts (tst_visual.qml /
# tools/uidriver.cpp), written for human eyeballing, never read by tests.
# The canonical output location is build/screenshots; these entries cover
# runs that wrote into the source tree instead. screenshots/press/ is the
# exception: curated, committed capture assets referenced by the README
# and the AppStream metadata, and screenshots/demo-vault/, the checked-in
# vault those stills are captured from (tools/capture-press-stills.sh).
# screenshots/gallery/ holds the feature-gallery clips gallery.md shows, with
# screenshots/demo-vault-gallery/ the few extra notes those clips need
# (tools/record-gallery.sh); both are likewise committed.
/screenshots/*
!/screenshots/press/
!/screenshots/demo-vault/
!/screenshots/demo-vault-gallery/
!/screenshots/gallery/
/tests/screenshots/
# Packaging outputs
dist/
packaging/linux/.tools/

# Local working material kept in this tree for convenience and never
# committed: launch and marketing planning, draft post copy, capture
# scratch. This entry is the only thing keeping it out of a commit, so do
# not add exceptions under it.
/planning/

# Coding-assistant instructions for this checkout, kept out of the tree for
# the same reason: they record this machine's environment rather than
# anything a reader of the repository needs. Contributor-facing build and
# test guidance belongs in devel.md and CONTRIBUTING.md, which are committed.
/CLAUDE.md
